P0033).\n    *   **U3_P03 (Sampling Obstacles):** Need atoms on standardization gaps (P0584/P0333, P0273, P0327, P0546).\n    *   **U4_P01 (Observational Strength & Intervention Hope):** Need FMT-LUMINate ORR (P0583), review of early trials (P0026, P0144, P0161, P0291, P0387, P0470, P0573).\n    *   **U4_P02 (Negative Intervention Trial):** Need MITRIC trial negative results (P0578).\n    *   **U4_P03 (Phase III Gap & Safety):** Need Phase III gap statement (P0584/P0333, P0273, P0583), Safety signals (Prevotella/Myocarditis in dual ICI) (P0583, P0260, P0462, P0600).\n    *   **T01 (Trial Comparison):** Need specific trial data atoms for FMT-LUMINate (P0583), MITRIC (P0578), MIMic (P0577), Early FMT/Probiotics (P0026, P0144, P0387).\n\n5.  **Drafting the Selection:**\n    *   I will iterate through the `evidence_atoms` list and pick the `atom_id`s that correspond to the `source_handle` and `field_path` values identified in the strategy above.\n    *   I must ensure I include atoms that represent limitations, negative results, and specific conditions (e.g., \"NIC arm\", \"HCC\", \"Phase II\", \"ORR 0%\").\n    *   I need to be careful not to miss atoms that provide the *context* for the findings (e.g., study design, sample size).\n\n    *   *Self-Correction on Atom IDs:* The input provides `atom_id`s like `atom::497bb7e33f801930e98c5290`. I need to copy these exactly.\n    *   *Coverage Check:* Ensure every task paragraph has supporting atoms.\n    *   *Balance Check:* Ensure negative results (MITRIC, HCC antibiotic null result) are included alongside positive ones (FMT-LUMINate).\n\n    *   *Specific Atom Selection:*\n        *   **U1:** P0096 (NSCLC review), P0146 (General review), P0298 (Meta-analysis), P0204 (HCC multi-kingdom), P0270 (mCRPC negative Akk), P0393 (Multi-kingdom), P0565 (Melanoma review), P0545 (Polish cohort), P0478 (Cross-cohort heterogeneity), P0170 (Enterotype), P0289 (Alpha diversity null), P0364 (Functional convergence), P0437 (Gene-level), P0